Keep the masked-tile skip of tiled flash attention off AMD only.

The skip reads the mask before a tile is staged or scored, with a
subgroupMax over the lanes and a shared row_live array. GCN/Vega wave64
devices run this tile shader for every decode step when the vec kernel is
off, and their subgroup ops are the ones that have miscompiled before: a
wrong live decision is a wrong attention sum, a tile wrongly skipped drops
real cells, a row wrongly skipped leaves stale sums.

The shader takes the skip only with a SKIP_MASKED_TILES define now, and
the pipeline adds that define for every adapter except AMD/ATI, which
ggml_webgpu_adapter_is_amd() recognizes. AMD compiles the tile shader as
it was before the skip: each tile is staged and scored, and a row is
bounded only by its own row_active, the decode of the shipped 1.3.0 build.
NVIDIA, Apple, Intel, and unknown vendors keep the skip of 0014 and pay
one string compare; the variant name records the difference.

diff --git a/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu-shader-lib.hpp b/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu-shader-lib.hpp
--- a/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu-shader-lib.hpp
+++ b/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu-shader-lib.hpp
@@ -115,6 +115,7 @@ struct ggml_webgpu_shader_lib_context {
     uint32_t    max_subgroup_size        = 0;
     bool        supports_dot_product     = false;
     std::string vendor;
+    std::string architecture;
 };
 
 struct webgpu_pipeline {
@@ -3022,6 +3023,12 @@ class ggml_webgpu_shader_lib {
             defines.push_back("MAX_SUBGROUP_SIZE=" + std::to_string(context.max_subgroup_size) + "u");
             variant += "_tile_sg" + std::to_string(context.min_subgroup_size) + "_" +
                        std::to_string(context.max_subgroup_size);
+            // The masked-tile skip is off AMD/ATI only; those adapters keep the tile
+            // shader that stages and scores every tile.
+            if (!ggml_webgpu_adapter_is_amd(context.vendor, context.architecture)) {
+                defines.push_back("SKIP_MASKED_TILES");
+                variant += "_skipmt";
+            }
         } else {
             shader_src = wgsl_flash_attn;
             defines.push_back(std::string("SG_MAT_M=") + std::to_string(context.sg_mat_m));
